cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use stentFIT in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "stentFIT: Semi-Automated Virtual Stent Implantation with Mixed-Dimensional Modelling"
abstract: >-
  stentFIT turns a stent surface mesh (.stl) into a 1D beam-element model ready
  for beam-to-solid contact simulation. It samples the stent surface, detects its
  rings, extracts a 2D skeleton from each ring, wraps that skeleton back onto the
  3D mid-surface, fits a B-spline to each strut curve, and meshes the result into
  Simo-Reissner beams. From that mesh it writes schema-validated 4C simulation
  input files, solves them in a pinned container, and measures the stent response.
  It also generates parametric test arteries and a catheter balloon to expand
  the stent through contact.
type: software
